### Topic 49 - JWT Authentication
### VS Code "REST Client" extension. Start the app first: mvn spring-boot:run
### Seeded users: admin / admin123 (ADMIN)   alice / alice123 (USER)
###
### The "# @name login" line names a request so later requests can reuse its response:
###   {{login.response.body.accessToken}}  -> the token from the login response. No copy-paste!

@host = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Login as alice -> 200 + token
# @name login
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice",
  "password": "alice123"
}

### 2. Call a protected endpoint WITH the token -> 200
GET {{host}}/api/hello
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### 3. Orders of the current user -> 200
GET {{host}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### 4. Same endpoint WITHOUT a token -> 401
GET {{host}}/api/hello

### 5. With a fake token -> 401
GET {{host}}/api/hello
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJoYWNrZXIifQ.invalidsignature

### 6. alice (USER) on the admin URL -> 403
GET {{host}}/api/admin/dashboard
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### 7. Login as admin -> 200 + token
# @name adminLogin
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "admin123"
}

### 8. Admin dashboard with the admin token -> 200
GET {{host}}/api/admin/dashboard
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 9. Wrong password -> 401
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice",
  "password": "nope"
}

### 10. Register a new user -> 201 + token (registered = logged in)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "bob",
  "password": "bob12345"
}
